{"questions":[{"question_id":"mnswhx9w","content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p><b>Statement I :</b> Sodium dichromate and potassium dichromate are classified as primary standards in titrimetric analysis.</p>\n<p><b>Statement II :</b> Phenolphthalein is a weak base, therefore it dissociates in acidic medium.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>\n","chapter":"ionic-equilibrium","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2026-online-5th-april-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift","permalink":"pgiven-below-are-two-statementsp-pstatement-i-sodiu-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-q55aa8qktsxcklor","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p><b>Statement I :</b> Sodium dichromate and potassium dichromate are classified as primary standards in titrimetric analysis.</p>\n<p><b>Statement II :</b> Phenolphthalein is a weak base, therefore it dissociates in acidic medium.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>\n","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>Both Statement I and Statement II are ture</p>\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>Both Statement I and Statement II are false</p>\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>Statement I is true but Statement II is false</p>\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>Statement I is false but Statement II is true</p>"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p><strong>Analysis of Statement I :</strong></p>\n<p>In titrimetric analysis, a primary standard is a substance of high purity that is stable and not hygroscopic, meaning its exact mass can be weighed directly to prepare a standard solution. According to NCERT, potassium dichromate (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.35ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4132.7 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(882,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1285.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2045.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2933.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is stable and non-hygroscopic, making it a good primary standard. </p>\n<p>However, sodium dichromate (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.635ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4700.7 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(562,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1853.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2613.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3501.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is highly hygroscopic (deliquescent). It readily absorbs moisture from the atmosphere, which changes its mass continuously. Due to this property, it cannot be weighed accurately to prepare a standard solution. Therefore, sodium dichromate is not classified as a primary standard. </p>\n<p>Because of the incorrect claim about sodium dichromate, <strong>Statement I is false</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Analysis of Statement II :</strong></p>\n<p>Phenolphthalein is an indicator widely used in acid-base titrations. Chemically, it is a weak organic acid, not a weak base. We often represent it as <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.011ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 2215 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1639,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. </p>\n<p>Since phenolphthalein is a weak acid, its dissociation is governed by the following equilibrium:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"19.292ex\" height=\"1.939ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 8527.1 857.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1639,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2492.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"21CC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-V-21CC\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(3770.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5566.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6567,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(7318,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(609,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>In an acidic medium, there is already an excess of hydrogen ions (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.561ex\" height=\"1.754ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1574 775.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). According to Le Chatelier's principle (specifically the common ion effect), the high concentration of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.561ex\" height=\"1.754ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1574 775.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> suppresses the dissociation of the weak acid <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.011ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 2215 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1639,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, causing it to remain mostly in its undissociated, colourless form. It is in a basic medium that phenolphthalein actually dissociates to form the pink-coloured <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.435ex\" height=\"1.779ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1960.1 786.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(751,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(609,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ion. </p>\n<p>Because phenolphthalein is a weak acid and does not dissociate significantly in an acidic medium, <strong>Statement II is false</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Conclusion :</strong></p>\n<p>Since both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect, the correct option is Option B.</p>\n<p><strong>Correct Answer :</strong></p>\n<p>Option B: Both Statement I and Statement II are false</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>नीचे दो कथन दिए गए हैं:</p>\n<p>कथन I: सोडियम डाइक्रोमेट एवं पोटेशियम डाइक्रोमेट को अनुमापनी विश्लेषण में प्राथमिक मानकों के रूप में वर्गीकृत किया जाता है।</p>\n<p>कथन II: फ़ीनॉलफ्थैलिन एक दुर्बल क्षार है, इसलिए यह अम्लीय माध्यम में वियोजित हो जाता है।</p>\n<p>उपर्युक्त कथनों के आलोक में, नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सही उत्तर चुनें:</p>\n\n\n","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>कथन I और कथन II दोनों सत्य हैं।</p>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>कथन I और ���थन II दोनों असत्य हैं।</p>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>कथन I सत्य है परन्तु कथन II असत्य है।</p>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>कथन I असत्य है परन्तु कथन II सत्य है।</p>\n"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p><strong>कथन I का विश्लेषण:</strong></p>\n<p>अनुमापन विश्लेषण (titrimetric analysis) में, एक प्राथमिक मानक (primary standard) उच्च शुद्धता वाला पदार्थ होता है जो स्थिर होता है और आर्द्रताग्राही (hygroscopic) नहीं होता है, जिसका अर्थ है कि एक मानक विलयन तैयार करने के लिए इसके सटीक द्रव्यमान को सीधे तौला जा सकता है। NCERT के अनुसार, पोटेशियम डाइक्रोमेट (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.35ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4132.7 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(882,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1285.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2045.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2933.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) स्थिर और गैर-आर्द्रताग्राही (non-hygroscopic) होता है, जो इसे एक अच्छा प्राथमिक मानक बनाता है। </p>\n<p>हालाँकि, सोडियम डाइक्रोमेट (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.635ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4700.7 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(562,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1853.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2613.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3501.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) अत्यधिक आर्द्रताग्राही (प्रस्वेद्य या deliquescent) होता है। यह वायुमंडल से आसानी से नमी सोख लेता है, जिससे इसका द्रव्यमान लगातार बदलता रहता है। इस गुण के कारण, मानक विलयन तैयार करने के लिए इसे सटीक रूप से नहीं तौला जा सकता है। इसलिए, सोडियम डाइक्रोमेट को प्राथमिक मानक के रूप में वर्गीकृत नहीं किया गया है। </p>\n<p>सोडियम डाइक्रोमेट के बारे में गलत दावे के कारण, <strong>कथन I गलत है</strong>।</p>\n<p><strong>कथन II का विश्लेषण:</strong></p>\n<p>अम्ल-क्षार अनुमापन (acid-base titrations) में फिनोलफ्थेलिन एक व्यापक रूप से उपयोग किया जाने वाला सूचक (indicator) है। रासायनिक रूप से, यह एक दुर्बल कार्बनिक अम्ल (weak organic acid) है, न कि दुर्बल क्षार। हम इसे अक्सर <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.011ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 2215 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1639,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> के रूप में दर्शाते हैं। </p>\n<p>चूँकि फिनोलफ्थेलिन एक दुर्बल अम्ल है, इसलिए इसका वियोजन (dissociation) निम्नलिखित साम्यावस्था (equilibrium) द्वारा नियंत्रित होता है:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"19.292ex\" height=\"1.939ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 8527.1 857.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1639,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2492.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"21CC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-V-21CC\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(3770.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5566.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6567,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(7318,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(609,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>अम्लीय माध्यम (acidic medium) में, पहले से ही हाइड्रोजन आयनों (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.561ex\" height=\"1.754ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1574 775.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) की अधिकता होती है। ले शातेलिए के नियम (Le Chatelier's principle) के अनुसार (विशेष रूप से सम-आयन प्रभाव या common ion effect), <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.561ex\" height=\"1.754ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1574 775.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> की उच्च सांद्रता दुर्बल अम्ल <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.011ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 2215 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1639,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> के वियोजन को दबा देती है, जिससे यह ज्यादातर अपने अवियोजित (undissociated) रंगहीन रूप में रहता है। क्षारीय माध्यम में ही फिनोलफ्थेलिन वास्तव में गुलाबी रंग का <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.435ex\" height=\"1.779ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1960.1 786.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(751,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(609,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> आयन बनाने के लिए वियोजित होता है। </p>\n<p>चूँकि फिनोलफ्थेलिन एक दुर्बल अम्ल है और अम्लीय माध्यम में पर्याप्त रूप से वियोजित नहीं होता है, इसलिए <strong>कथन II गलत है</strong>।</p>\n<p><strong>निष्कर्ष:</strong></p>\n<p>चूँकि कथन I और कथन II दोनों गलत हैं, इसलिए सही विकल्प, विकल्प B है।</p>\n<p><strong>सही उत्तर:</strong></p>\n<p>विकल्प B: कथन I और कथन II दोनों गलत हैं</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","timeAllotted":144000,"topic":"ph-buffer-and-indicators","type":"mcq","year":2026,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-main-2026-online-5th-april-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>Both Statement I and Statement II are ture</p>\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>Both Statement I and Statement II are false</p>\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>Statement I is true but Statement II is false</p>\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>Statement I is false but Statement II is true</p>"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p><strong>Analysis of Statement I :</strong></p>\n<p>In titrimetric analysis, a primary standard is a substance of high purity that is stable and not hygroscopic, meaning its exact mass can be weighed directly to prepare a standard solution. According to NCERT, potassium dichromate (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.35ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4132.7 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(882,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1285.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2045.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2933.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is stable and non-hygroscopic, making it a good primary standard. </p>\n<p>However, sodium dichromate (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.635ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4700.7 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(562,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1853.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2613.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3501.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is highly hygroscopic (deliquescent). It readily absorbs moisture from the atmosphere, which changes its mass continuously. Due to this property, it cannot be weighed accurately to prepare a standard solution. Therefore, sodium dichromate is not classified as a primary standard. </p>\n<p>Because of the incorrect claim about sodium dichromate, <strong>Statement I is false</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Analysis of Statement II :</strong></p>\n<p>Phenolphthalein is an indicator widely used in acid-base titrations. Chemically, it is a weak organic acid, not a weak base. We often represent it as <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.011ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 2215 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1639,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. </p>\n<p>Since phenolphthalein is a weak acid, its dissociation is governed by the following equilibrium:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"19.292ex\" height=\"1.939ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 8527.1 857.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1639,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2492.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"21CC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-V-21CC\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(3770.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5566.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6567,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(7318,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(609,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>In an acidic medium, there is already an excess of hydrogen ions (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.561ex\" height=\"1.754ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1574 775.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). According to Le Chatelier's principle (specifically the common ion effect), the high concentration of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.561ex\" height=\"1.754ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1574 775.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> suppresses the dissociation of the weak acid <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.011ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 2215 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1639,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, causing it to remain mostly in its undissociated, colourless form. It is in a basic medium that phenolphthalein actually dissociates to form the pink-coloured <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.435ex\" height=\"1.779ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1960.1 786.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(751,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(609,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ion. </p>\n<p>Because phenolphthalein is a weak acid and does not dissociate significantly in an acidic medium, <strong>Statement II is false</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Conclusion :</strong></p>\n<p>Since both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect, the correct option is Option B.</p>\n<p><strong>Correct Answer :</strong></p>\n<p>Option B: Both Statement I and Statement II are false</p>"}]}